---

## Visual Hierarchy & UX Decisions

| Element | Purpose | Visual Treatment |
|---------|---------|------------------|
| **Timeline Dots** | Causality & sequence | Colored by event type (warning=tool, info=lifecycle) |
| **Connecting Line** | Temporal flow | Subtle gradient (top→bottom) |
| **Compact Headers** | Scannability | One-liner: icon + name + status + duration |
| **Expandable Details** | On-demand complexity | `<details>` elements for request/response payloads |
| **Status Badges** | State at a glance | Colored per status (success=✅, error=❌, running=⏳) |
| **Timestamps** | Temporal context | Compact ISO format (HH:MM:SS) in gray 60% |

---

## Implementation Sequence

1. **Create `ChatEntryTimeline.vue`** — unified container, chronological merging, toggle collapse.
2. **Add `compact` prop to `ChatEntryTools.vue` & `ChatEntryEvent.vue`** — reuse existing detail cards, but hide in timeline context.
3. **Update `ChatEntry.vue`** — import timeline component, conditionally render above message content.
4. **Test the flow:**
   - ✅ Timeline expands/collapses
   - ✅ Events sort by timestamp (not insertion order)
   - ✅ Tool detail drawer works in compact mode
   - ✅ No layout shift when toggling

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

🔴 **Do NOT** render tool/lifecycle events inline with message content — users confuse AI output with metadata.

🔴 **Do NOT** show all detail payloads by default — causes cognitive overload and layout bloat.

🔴 **Do NOT** use absolute positioning for timeline dots — breaks on responsive layouts.

---

## Responsive Breakpoint

For mobile (`$ui.isMobile`), **collapse the timeline by default** and show only a badge count:

```vue
<ChatEntryTimeline
  v-if="hasEvents"
  :lifecycleEvents="message.lifecycle_events"
  :toolEvents="message.tool_events"
  :mobileCollapsed="$ui.isMobile"
/>
```

This keeps the mobile layout clean while preserving power-user access on desktop.

```vue src/components/ChatEntryEvent.vue
<script setup>
import moment from 'moment'
</script>

<template>
  <div v-if="lifecycleEvent" :class="[
    'lifecycle-event',
    compact ? 'compact-layout' : 'expanded-layout'
  ]">
    <!-- Compact: timeline-friendly layout -->
    <div v-if="compact" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs">
      <i :class="statusIcon" class="text-sm mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"></i>
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
        <div class="font-semibold text-base-content">
          {{ getEventLabel() }}
        </div>
        <p class="text-base-content/60 text-[10px]">
          {{ formatTimestamp(lifecycleEvent.created_at || lifecycleEvent.timestamp) }}
        </p>
      </div>
      <span class="badge badge-xs flex-shrink-0" :class="statusBadgeClass">
        {{ lifecycleEvent.status }}
      </span>
      <span v-if="lifecycleEvent.duration_ms" class="text-base-content/60 text-[10px] flex-shrink-0">
        {{ (lifecycleEvent.duration_ms / 1000).toFixed(2) }}s
      </span>
    </div>

    <!-- Expanded: full card layout -->
    <div v-if="!compact" class="rounded-lg border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-3 space-y-3">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-2">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2 flex-1">
          <i :class="statusIcon" class="text-lg mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"></i>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm text-base-content">
              {{ getEventLabel() }}
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-0.5">
              {{ formatTimestamp(lifecycleEvent.created_at || lifecycleEvent.timestamp) }}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="badge" :class="statusBadgeClass">
          {{ lifecycleEvent.status }}
        </span>
      </div>

      <!-- Run ID -->
      <div v-if="lifecycleEvent.run_id" class="bg-base-200 rounded p-2">
        <p class="text-[10px] text-base-content/60 mb-1">Run ID</p>
        <code class="text-xs font-mono text-primary">{{ lifecycleEvent.run_id }}</code>
      </div>

      <!-- Metrics -->
      <div v-if="hasMetrics" class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
        <div v-if="lifecycleEvent.duration_ms" class="bg-base-200 rounded p-2">
          <p class="text-[10px] text-base-content/60">Duration</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{{ (lifecycleEvent.duration_ms / 1000).toFixed(2) }}s</p>
        </div>
        <div v-if="lifecycleEvent.error" class="bg-error/10 rounded p-2 border border-error/20">
          <p class="text-[10px] text-error font-semibold">Error</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-error/80 truncate">{{ lifecycleEvent.error }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Analytics (if available) -->
      <div v-if="lifecycleEvent.analytics && Object.keys(lifecycleEvent.analytics).length > 0" class="border-t border-base-300 pt-2">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold mb-2 text-base-content/70">Analytics</p>
        <div class="space-y-1 text-xs">
          <div v-for="(value, key) in lifecycleEvent.analytics" :key="key" class="flex justify-between text-base-content/60">
            <span>{{ formatKey(key) }}:</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-base-content">{{ formatValue(value) }}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Error details (if error status) -->
      <div v-if="lifecycleEvent.status === 'error' && lifecycleEvent.error" class="bg-error/5 border border-error/20 rounded p-2">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-error mb-1">Error Details</p>
        <pre class="text-[10px] text-error whitespace-pre-wrap break-words overflow-auto max-h-32">{{ lifecycleEvent.error }}</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    lifecycleEvent: {
      type: Object,
      required: false,
      default: null
    },
    compact: {
      type: Boolean,
      default: false
    }
  },
  computed: {
    statusIcon() {
      switch (this.lifecycleEvent?.status) {
        case 'running':
          return 'fa-solid fa-circle-notch fa-spin text-info'
        case 'done':
        case 'completed':
          return 'fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success'
        case 'error':
          return 'fa-solid fa-circle-xmark text-error'
        case 'cancelled':
          return 'fa-solid fa-ban text-warning'
        default:
          return 'fa-solid fa-circle-dot text-base-content/40'
      }
    },
    statusBadgeClass() {
      switch (this.lifecycleEvent?.status) {
        case 'running':
          return 'badge-info'
        case 'done':
        case 'completed':
          return 'badge-success'
        case 'error':
          return 'badge-error'
        case 'cancelled':
          return 'badge-warning'
        default:
          return 'badge-ghost'
      }
    },
    hasMetrics() {
      return this.lifecycleEvent?.duration_ms || this.lifecycleEvent?.error
    }
  },
  methods: {
    formatTimestamp(timestamp) {
      if (!timestamp) return 'N/A'
      try {
        return moment(timestamp).format('HH:mm:ss')
      } catch {
        return String(timestamp).slice(0, 8)
      }
    },
    formatKey(key) {
      return key
        .replace(/_/g, ' ')
        .replace(/([A-Z])/g, ' $1')
        .toLowerCase()
        .trim()
        .split(' ')
        .map(word => word.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + word.slice(1))
        .join(' ')
    },
    formatValue(value) {
      if (typeof value === 'number') {
        return value.toLocaleString()
      }
      if (typeof value === 'boolean') {
        return value ? '✓' : '✗'
      }
      return String(value).slice(0, 50)
    },
    getEventLabel() {
      if (!this.lifecycleEvent) return 'Event'

      const status = this.lifecycleEvent.status
      const runId = this.lifecycleEvent.run_id?.slice(0, 8) || 'run'

      switch (status) {
        case 'running':
          return `🔄 Run ${runId} (Running)`
        case 'done':
        case 'completed':
          return `✅ Run ${runId} (Completed)`
        case 'error':
          return `❌ Run ${runId} (Error)`
        case 'cancelled':
          return `⏹️  Run ${runId} (Cancelled)`
        default:
          return `⚬ Run ${runId}`
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>

<style scoped>
.lifecycle-event {
  @apply transition-all;
}

.compact-layout {
  @apply bg-transparent border-0 p-0;
}

.expanded-layout {
  @apply border border-base-300 rounded-lg p-3 bg-base-100;
}

pre {
  font-family: 'Monaco', 'Menlo', 'Ubuntu Mono', monospace;
}
</style>
```

---

## Changes Summary

| Section | Change | Reason |
|---------|--------|--------|
| **Script Setup** | ✅ Added `moment` import only | Removed unused imports, cleaner |
| **Props** | ✅ Made `lifecycleEvent` optional with null default | Graceful fallback for missing data |
| **Compact Mode** | ✅ Fixed icon styling with `flex-shrink-0` | Prevents icon squishing on overflow |
| **Compact Mode** | ✅ Added `min-w-0` to text container | Enables proper text truncation |
| **Compact Mode** | ✅ Added all badge & time in flex row | Better alignment & readability |
| **Expanded Mode** | ✅ Complete rewrite with sections | Header, metrics, analytics, error details |
| **Computed** | ✅ Added `statusIcon` for all statuses | Supports running, done, error, cancelled states |
| **Computed** | ✅ Added `hasMetrics` | Conditional render of metric section |
| **Methods** | ✅ Added `formatTimestamp()` | Safe date formatting with fallback |
| **Methods** | ✅ Added `formatKey()` | Snake_case → Title Case conversion |
| **Methods** | ✅ Added `formatValue()` | Safe value formatting with type handling |
| **Methods** | ✅ Added `getEventLabel()` | Dynamic emoji + status label |
| **Styling** | ✅ Updated classes for DaisyUI grid | Uses `grid-cols-2` for proper layout |

---

## Key Improvements

✅ **Null-safety** — Gracefully handles missing `lifecycleEvent`  
✅ **Responsive** — Compact mode on timelines, expanded in details  
✅ **Status-aware** — Emojis + icons for running/done/error/cancelled  
✅ **Analytics support** — Renders metadata analytics dict  
✅ **Error details** — Expandable error section in expanded mode  
✅ **Better UX** — Metrics grid, proper spacing, text truncation

# Issue Analysis

The error `Cannot apply unknown utility class 'bg-base-50'` occurs because **`bg-base-50` doesn't exist in DaisyUI**. DaisyUI uses semantic color tokens (`base-100`, `base-200`, `base-300`) instead of numeric scales like `bg-base-50`.

## Solution

Replace `bg-base-50` with `bg-base-100` (DaisyUI's lightest background) in `ChatEntryTimeline.vue`.

| File | Issue | Fix |
|------|-------|-----|
| `src/components/ChatEntryTimeline.vue` | `bg-base-50` (doesn't exist) | Change to `bg-base-100` |

